    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23071" root="شمل" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُشْتَمِلٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَمِلٌ</span> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  One says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَآءَ مُشْتَمِلًا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِسَيْفِهِ</span> like as one says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْتَدِيًا</span> [i. e. <i>He came
having his sword hung upon him</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَآءَ فُلَانٌ مُشْتَمِلًا عَلَى دَاهِيَةٍ</span> (tropical:)  [<i>Such a one
came conceiving a calamity</i>]. (TA.)

